            "type": "MCQ",
            "text": "<span style=\"display: inline;\"><div itemprop=\"text\"><p>Consider the following context-free grammar $G$, where $S, X$, and $Y$ are the variables (nonterminals), $a, b$, and $c$ are the terminal symbols, $S$ is the start variable, and the rules of $G$ are described as:</p><p>$$<br/>\\begin{aligned}<br/>&amp; S \\rightarrow a X \\mid Y c \\\\<br/>&amp; X \\rightarrow a X b \\mid a b \\\\<br/>&amp; Y \\rightarrow b Y c \\mid b c<br/>\\end{aligned}<br/>$$</p><p><br/>Which ONE of the following languages $L(G)$ is generated by $G$ ?</p></div></span>",
