        {
            "marks": 1,
            "neg": 0.33,
            "type": "MCQ",
            "text": "<span style=\"display: inline;\"><div itemprop=\"text\"><p>What language $L$ is generated by the following regular grammar? (Assume $S$ is the start symbol).</p><p>$$<br/>\\begin{aligned}<br/>&amp; S \\rightarrow a A \\\\<br/>&amp; A \\rightarrow a A|a B| \\lambda \\\\<br/>&amp; B \\rightarrow b A<br/>\\end{aligned}<br/>$$</p></div></span>",
            "image": "",
            "options": [
                "<span style=\"display: inline;\">$L=a a^*(a b+a)^*$<br/></span>",
                "<span style=\"display: inline;\">$L=a\\left(a^* b^*+a^*\\right)$<br/></span>",
                "<span style=\"display: inline;\">$L=a(a+b)^* a b$<br/></span>",
                "<span style=\"display: inline;\">$L=a^* a(a+b)^*$</span>"
            ],
            "answer": "A",
            "solution": "<div style=\"background-color: #bae1c4; border: 1px solid #75c98a; border-radius: 10px; padding: 10px 15px; margin-top: 15px; color: #155724; font-family: sans-serif;\">  <strong style=\"font-size: 16px; color: #000;\">Explanation:</strong><br> <a name=\"493894\"></a><div itemprop=\"text\"><p>Let's find the language by substitution, starting from the non-terminating rules $A$ and $B$.<br/><br/>The language generated from $A$, let's call it $L(A)$, is defined by the rules:</p><ul><li>$A \\rightarrow a A$ (can prefix any number of 'a's)<br/> </li><li>$A \\rightarrow a B$ (can prefix an 'a' and go to $B$ )<br/> </li><li>$A \\rightarrow \\lambda$ (can terminate)<br/> </li><li>The rule for $B$ is $B \\rightarrow b A$. This means $B$ must produce a ' $b$ ' and then return to $A$.</li></ul><p>If we substitute $B$ back into $A$ 's rules, we get: $A \\rightarrow a A|a(b A)| \\lambda A \\rightarrow a A|a b A| \\lambda$<br/><br/>This can be rewritten using a Kleene star. This is a classic recursive definition: $L(A)=(a+ a b)^* L(A)+\\lambda$<br/><br/>This simplifies to $L(A)=(a+a b)^*$.<br/><br/>$S \\rightarrow a A$</p><p>$$<br/>\\begin{aligned}<br/>&amp; L=a \\cdot L(A) \\\\<br/>&amp; L=a(a+a b)^*<br/>\\end{aligned}<br/>$$</p><p><br/>Now we must check if $L=a(a+a b)^*$ is equivalent to Option A, $L^{\\prime}=a a^*(a b+a)^*$.<br/>We can use the regular expression identity:<br/> <br/>$\\mathbf{R}_1^*\\left(\\mathbf{R}_2+\\mathbf{R}_1\\right)^*=\\left(\\mathbf{R}_1+\\mathbf{R}_2\\right)^*$.</p><ul><li>Let's look at Option A: $L^{\\prime}=a \\cdot a^* \\cdot(a b+a)^*$<br/> </li><li>Let $R_1=a$ and $R_2=a b$.<br/> </li><li>The expression $a^* \\cdot(a b+a)^*$ matches the identity $R_1^* \\cdot\\left(R_2+R_1\\right)^*$.<br/> </li><li>Therefore, $a^*(a b+a)^*=(a+a b)^*$.<br/> </li><li>By substituting this back into $L^{\\prime}$, we get: $L^{\\prime}=a \\cdot(a+a b)^*$</li></ul><p>This proves that $L=L^{\\prime}$, so the grammar generates the language $a a^*(a b+a)^*$.</p><p><strong>Hence A is correct</strong></p></div><br><br><a href=\"https://gateoverflow.in/493893/go-classes-dpp-toc-grammar#a_list\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"text-decoration: none; color: #2e7bc5; font-size: 15px;\">Click here for detail solution by gateoverflow</a><div class=\"year_sub_chap_link\" style=\"margin-top:5px; font-size:14px;\"><b><a href=\"https://gateoverflow.in/tag/goclasses-toc-practice-questions\" style=\"color:#2f6d1a; text-decoration:none\" target=\"_blank\">GO Classes DPP</a></b> <b><a href=\"https://gateoverflow.in/tag/theory-of-computation\" style=\"color:#2f6d1a; text-decoration:none\" target=\"_blank\">TOC - Context Free Grammar</a></b></div></div>"
        },
        {
            "marks": 1,
            "neg": 0.33,
            "type": "MCQ",
            "text": "<span style=\"display: inline;\"><div itemprop=\"text\"><p>What is the minimum number of states required in a Deterministic Finite Automaton (DFA) to accept the language generated by the following grammar?<br/><br/>$S \\rightarrow a b A$<br/><br/>$A \\rightarrow b a B$<br/><br/>$B \\rightarrow a A \\mid b b$<br/> </p></div></span>",
            "image": "",
            "options": [
                "<span style=\"display: inline;\">$6$<br/></span>",
                "<span style=\"display: inline;\">$7$<br/></span>",
                "<span style=\"display: inline;\">$8$<br/></span>",
                "<span style=\"display: inline;\">$9$</span>"
            ],
            "answer": "A",
            "solution": "<div style=\"background-color: #bae1c4; border: 1px solid #75c98a; border-radius: 10px; padding: 10px 15px; margin-top: 15px; color: #155724; font-family: sans-serif;\">  <strong style=\"font-size: 16px; color: #000;\">Explanation:</strong><br> <a name=\"493892\"></a><div itemprop=\"text\">the language is $L=\\mathbf{a b}(\\mathbf{b a a})^* \\mathbf{b a b b}$.<br/> <br/> Min dfa will have $8$ states for this language.</div><br><br><a href=\"https://gateoverflow.in/493891/go-classes-dpp-toc-min-dfa#a_list\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"text-decoration: none; color: #2e7bc5; font-size: 15px;\">Click here for detail solution by gateoverflow</a><div class=\"year_sub_chap_link\" style=\"margin-top:5px; font-size:14px;\"><b><a href=\"https://gateoverflow.in/tag/goclasses-toc-practice-questions\" style=\"color:#2f6d1a; text-decoration:none\" target=\"_blank\">GO Classes DPP</a></b> <b><a href=\"https://gateoverflow.in/tag/theory-of-computation\" style=\"color:#2f6d1a; text-decoration:none\" target=\"_blank\">TOC - Context Free Grammar</a></b></div></div>"
        }
